      "message": "fix(ui): hold the playhead while the stock removal is calculated\n\nThe playback worker calculates the whole stock removal before it\npublishes a frame (#2181). During that time the viewport shows the\nuncut stock, but the transport clock played on: the tool moved over\nstock that showed no cut, and on a large block the whole program could\nplay with no visible removal.\n\nThe transport now holds its playhead and disables the scrub slider\nwhile the calculation runs, as its line already says. Cancel ends the\ncalculation and playback cuts live, as before.\n\nA new app test proves that the worker's frames draw the removal as the\nprogram plays, at the full and at the display budget.\n\nFixes #2611\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
